\@writefile{lof}{\contentsline {figure}{\numberline {5.11}{\ignorespaces \texttt  {simp} and \texttt  {simp\_once}: the fixpoint loop and its two non-trivial cases. \texttt  {collect\_alt\_branches}, \texttt  {dedup\_first}, and \texttt  {fold\_alt} implement flattening, deduplication, and rebuilding an $n$-ary alternation, omitted here for space; each does no more than its name says. \texttt  {fuse\_bits} is \texttt  {fuse}'s (\S  \ref {sec:fuse}) counterpart for the native \texttt  {Bits} type, avoiding a conversion back to a slice that would force the entire accumulated history to be materialized.}}{37}{figure.caption.26}\protected@file@percent }
